        {
            "sentence_index": 21,
            "timestamp": {
                "start": 125.18,
                "end": 171.54
            },
            "transcript": "Beneath some foreign arch of sky, how many a time the rover you were I, for life off -sundered look from look, and voice from voice, the transient earth schooling my soul, to brook this distance that no messages may span, would chance upon our wilding by a lonely well, or drowsy watermelon, or swaying to the chime of convent bell, or where the nightingales of old romance with tragic contraltoes, failed dim solitudes of infinite desire, and once I joyed to meet our peasant gait about, a trespasser on trim, signorial seat, twinkling a saucy eye as potentates paste by.",
            "acoustic_emotion": {
                "angry": 0.5963297694366712,
                "calm": 1.960951758121426,
